  • Field_1, being the lowest-threat area and with limited resources overall, is left without a dedicated drone group since our available drones are better used where the risk is higher.

6. Finally, we assign each drone to exactly one group. The drones that were originally protecting Field_4 remain there as required; the others are reassigned as follows:
  • Drone_1, Drone_2, Drone_3 → protecting Field_4,
  • Drone_4, Drone_8 → protecting Field_3,
  • Drone_5, Drone_6, Drone_7 → protecting Field_2.

This distribution concentrates our limited aerial resources on the fields with the higher threat levels (Fields 4, 3, and 2), thereby minimizing the potential overall damage on the farm.
